{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Going and growing very strong.</b> The way of an ordinary person — all the while that he prolongs his blast, his voice grows weaker and fainter; but here, it went and grew very strong. And why thus at the start? To accustom their ears to what they could hear." "<b>Moshe will speak.</b> When Moshe would speak and make the commandments heard to Israel — for they heard from the mouth of the Almighty only 'I am' and 'You shall not have' — the Holy One, blessed be He, would help him, to put strength in him so that his voice would carry and be heard (there)." "<b>Would answer him in a voice.</b> He would answer him concerning the voice, as in ״אֲשֶׁר יַעֲנֶה בָאֵשׁ״ (I Kings 18) — concerning the fire, to bring it down."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :register {:flags {1 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:10.994128031Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}